;; Task registry for `kbb --backend sci scripts/run-task.cljk <task> [args…]` (ADR-2607173000).
;;
;; Originally auto-generated from bb.edn; `:test` and `:render-test` were hand-ported afterwards
;; because bb.edn's removal left `kbb -M:test` / `kbb -M:render-test` with nothing to resolve them. See
;; scripts/tasks-complex.edn's remaining `:gen-presets` entry for what is still unported.
;;
;; `:render-test` was ported off `bb` for real in ADR-2608135000. It had been left as
;; `["sh" "-c" "cd ../webgpu && exec bb …"]` on the argument that its dependencies are JVM-only and
;; `bb` still works standalone. Two things were wrong with that. The binary is retired workspace-wide
;; and is not installed on murakumo fleet nodes, so the task could not run there at all; and "bb
;; still works" quietly meant "bb's BUNDLED libraries still work" — see :render-test's own note.
{:test
 ;; Data gate: every race × class × monster × skill composes to valid kami.sprite2d data.
 ;; test/chargen_test.cljk is a plain ns-less script (no (ns ...) form, no clojure.test) —
 ;; it's designed to be executed top-to-bottom, not required as a namespace, so it's passed
 ;; directly as nbb's script argument (nbb runs a .cljc file as a script the same way it runs
 ;; .cljs) rather than via `-e "(load-file ...)"` (a bb/JVM-ism nbb doesn't have).
 {:cmd ["kbb" "--backend" "sci" "--classpath" "src:test" "test/chargen_test.cljk"]}

 :render-test
 ;; Pixel-verified proof (real headless-Chromium WebGL2 readPixels) that a composed preset
 ;; actually draws — see test/render_pixel_test.cljk's own header comment for the full story.
 ;;
 ;; WHAT bb WAS HIDING. `kami.playwright` requires `babashka.process`, and the test requires
 ;; `cheshire.core`; babashka bundles both, so neither was ever declared anywhere. Under any other
 ;; runtime the very first require failed. `babashka.process` is a perfectly ordinary maven
 ;; artifact (babashka/process) and is declared below — the dependency was real, only its
 ;; declaration was missing, which is what a bundled runtime does to a dependency list.
 ;;
 ;; PRE-EXISTING FAILURE, NOT A PORT REGRESSION. This task exits 1. It runs the real pipeline and
 ;; reads real pixels; one of nine assertions fails — the protagonist's cheat-aura samples
 ;; [255 255 176] where the fixture pins [255 255 193] ±12. The identical failure was measured
 ;; under the old `bb` command before this port, so the port reproduces bb's behaviour exactly.
 ;; The likely cause is 4ce4469 (2026-07-23, :pixel8 palette + walk-cycle motion, which reworks
 ;; cheat-aura's prepended :pulse halos) landing 15 days AFTER the pin was recorded (5d8d208,
 ;; 2026-07-08) — during the window in which this task could not be run at all. It is deliberately
 ;; NOT "fixed" by widening the tolerance: the number is a pin, and a pin you move to make a test
 ;; pass is not a pin.
 ;;
 ;; :dir, not `sh -c "cd …"`. The test must run with the working directory set to the sibling
 ;; kotoba-lang/webgpu checkout, because kami.playwright's bridge (`scripts/pw_eval.cjs`) and the
 ;; sprite-SDF GLSL fixtures (`fixtures/glsl/`) are both read via cwd-relative paths. run-task.cljs
 ;; now takes :dir directly, so the real argv is visible in this file instead of buried in a shell
 ;; string where nothing that reads registries can see the command being run.
 ;;
 ;; The classpath names each sibling because kami.playwright/kami.scene2d/kami.sprite-gpu were each
 ;; split out of kotoba-lang/webgpu into their own repos, pulling further siblings transitively
 ;; (kami.scene2d → kami.sprite2d.layout in sprite2d; kami.sprite-gpu → kami.wgsl in wgsl →
 ;; kotoba.expr in expr). :replace-paths/:replace-deps rather than :extra-* so that webgpu's own
 ;; ~20 git deps are NOT resolved just to run this test — none are needed, and any one of them
 ;; carrying a broken pin would otherwise take this task down with it.
 ;; Sibling-checkout layout needed: orgs/kotoba-lang/{kami-isekai-assets,webgpu,playwright,scene2d,
 ;; sprite-gpu,sprite2d,wgsl,expr} — the layout west already checks these out in.
 {:dir "../webgpu"
  :cmd ["kbb" "-Sdeps"
        "{:aliases {:isekai-render-test {:replace-paths [\"../kami-isekai-assets/src\" \"src\" \"../playwright/src\" \"../scene2d/src\" \"../sprite-gpu/src\" \"../sprite2d/src\" \"../wgsl/src\" \"../expr/src\"] :replace-deps {org.clojure/clojure {:mvn/version \"1.12.0\"} cheshire/cheshire {:mvn/version \"5.13.0\"} babashka/process {:mvn/version \"0.5.22\"}} :main-opts [\"../kami-isekai-assets/test/render_pixel_test.cljk\"]}}}"
        "-M:isekai-render-test"]}}
